---
Title: Teriyaki Chicken Crockpot
Servings: 1
Tags: Prospects, Poultry, Asian
---

Pat the boneless @Chicken Thighs{2 pounds} dry with paper towels.

Heat @Butter{2 Tablespoons} ina #skillet and sear the Chicken for 3 minutes per side (does not need to be fully cooked).

Place sliced @Onions{1} in the bottom of the #Crockpot and arrange the Chicken on top.

Whisk together:
- @Shoyu{1/4 cup}
- @Water{1/4 cup}
- @Brown Sugar{1 cup}
- minced @Garlic{@Tablespoon}
- @Ginger{1 Tablespoon}
- @Seasame Oil{2 Tablespoons}
- @Rice Vinegar{2 Tablespoons}
- @Cornstarch{1 Tablespoon}
- @Gochugaru{1 Tablespoon}
- @Honey{1 teaspoon}

Pour the sauce over the Chicken and cook on low for 4-5 hours or high for 2-3 hours until the Chicken is tender and reaches at least 185°F internal temperature.

Optional: Last 30 minutes add other vegatables like @Broccoli, @Carrots, or @Bell Peppers{} to the Crockpot.

Serve the Chicken over @Rice{1.5 cups} and spoond that teriyaki sauce over everything.  Finish with a sprinkle of @Sesame Seeds{} and chopped @Green Onions{} for garnish.